---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LetterDialog from '../components/LetterDialog.astro';
import contacts from '../../data/contacts.json';
import rules from '../../data/rules.json';
const reviewRules=rules.filter(r=>['repudiation-review','deduction-reasons','grievance-14-days'].includes(r.id));
---
<Base title="Review a rejected claim — ClaimClock"><div class="wrap"><section class="page-hero"><p class="eyebrow" data-i18n="rejection.eyebrow">A WRITTEN REASON. A CLEAR NEXT STEP.</p><h1 data-i18n="rejection.title">Ask for a review of your rejected claim.</h1><p class="lead" data-i18n="rejection.body">Prepare a formal grievance to your insurer. Your details stay in this page until you choose to share the letter.</p></section><div class="index-columns"><div class="stack"><section class="card"><h2 data-i18n="rejection.details">Start with the rejection letter</h2><form id="rejection-form" class="form-grid"><label class="full"><span data-i18n="rejection.upload">Rejection letter (optional PDF or photo — read on this device)</span><input type="file" id="rejection-file" accept="application/pdf,image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp" /><small class="status" id="rejection-extract-status" role="status"></small></label><label class="full"><span data-i18n="label.insurer">Your insurer</span><select data-searchable name="insurer" required><option value="" data-i18n="label.choose">Choose your insurer</option>{contacts.filter(c=>c.kind==='insurer').sort((a,b)=>a.name.localeCompare(b.name)).map(c=><option value={c.id} data-search={c.name_hi}>{c.name}</option>)}</select></label><label class="full"><span data-i18n="rejection.date">Date the rejection was communicated to you</span><input name="rejectedOn" type="date" required /></label><label class="full"><span data-i18n="rejection.ground">Reason given for rejection</span><textarea name="ground" rows="6" maxlength="2000" required></textarea></label><p class="fine-print full" data-i18n="rejection.private">Copy the stated reason without names or policy numbers. Add identifying details yourself to the final letter. Reload or close this page to clear your entries.</p><button type="submit" class="button full" disabled data-i18n="rejection.prepare">Prepare GRO representation</button><p id="rejection-status" class="error full" role="alert"></p></form></section><section class="card"><h2 data-i18n="rejection.sources">What your request relies on</h2>{reviewRules.map(r=><details><summary>{r.paragraph}</summary><p>“{r.quote}”</p><p data-i18n={`rejection.rule.${r.id}`}>{r.plain_en}</p><a href={r.source_url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="rejection.source">Read the primary source ↗</a></details>)}</section></div><aside class="stack"><section class="card rights-card"><h2 data-i18n="rejection.next">Keep the next steps clear</h2><ol><li><p data-i18n="rejection.gro">Send your grievance to the insurer’s GRO. Keep the acknowledgement and attachments. The insurer should resolve the complaint within 14 days.</p></li><li><p data-i18n="rejection.bima">If unresolved, you can raise a complaint on Bima Bharosa. Keep its token. The insured or claimant files the complaint.</p><a href="https://bimabharosa.irdai.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bima Bharosa ↗</a></li><li><p data-i18n="rejection.ombudsman">First complain to the insurer. An unsatisfactory or rejected grievance response, or no reply for one calendar month, can open the free Insurance Ombudsman route. One month is not always 30 days. File within one year of the applicable response or the expiry of that month. The limit is ₹50 lakh including expenses; check all eligibility conditions.</p><a href="https://www.cioins.co.in/Faqs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-i18n="rejection.eligibility">Check Ombudsman eligibility ↗</a></li><li><p data-i18n="rejection.consumer">A Consumer Commission is another route; e-Jagriti is the online portal. The usual limit is two years from the cause of action. Check jurisdiction and dates. The same dispute must not be pending or decided in court, a consumer forum or arbitration for the Ombudsman route.</p><a href="https://e-jagriti.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">e-Jagriti ↗</a></li></ol></section><p class="notice" data-i18n="rejection.limit">A cashless refusal may differ from final claim repudiation. Ask the insurer which decision it made. This draft requests a review; it cannot decide coverage or guarantee payment.</p></aside></div><p class="fine-print" data-i18n="rejection.filing">You review, sign and send every complaint yourself. ClaimClock does not contact the insurer or file a case for you.</p><div class="empty-note"></div></div><LetterDialog/><script>import '../lib/rejection-ui';</script></Base>
